# What a deploy asks you for. Four values, and nothing else.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE PROMPT LIST. The "Deploy to Cloudflare" button reads it and
# asks for each name below as you deploy, so a one-click deploy ends with an
# instance that can actually reach a mailbox. That is why it holds exactly the
# values only you can supply -- and why nothing else may be added to it. A name
# in here becomes a question every deployer has to answer.
#
# In particular, NOT in here:
#   - the sizing knobs and LOG_LEVEL. They have committed defaults in the
#     `vars` block of wrangler.jsonc, where a deployer can see and change them.
#   - ACCESS_AUD. Setting it before the Access application exists and works is
#     the documented lockout (docs/authentication.md): it is the optional
#     upgrade AFTER a deploy, never a question during one.
#   - CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID / CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN. Those configure wrangler
#     itself, not the Worker; put them in a gitignored `.env` (see
#     docs/configuration.md).
#
# All four are set as Worker SECRETS. Two of them genuinely are secret; the
# host and the user are not, and are stored that way on purpose, because the
# secret store is the only place that is uncommitted (this repository is
# public, so a mailbox address cannot be committed), untouched by a deploy, and
# offered by the button's prompt. `env.IMAP_HOST` reads the same either way, so
# an instance that already sets them as `vars` keeps working unchanged.
#
# LOCALLY: copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill it in;
# `pnpm run dev` reads it. Values are left empty deliberately -- a blank is
# refused by name at startup, which is better than a plausible-looking default
# that silently points at the wrong mailbox.
#
# Once deployed, `GET /status` reports which of these are in effect (a secret
# cannot be read back out of the dashboard). See docs/observability.md.

# IMAP hostname. iCloud: imap.mail.me.com
IMAP_HOST=

# Mailbox user. For iCloud, LOGIN takes the LOCAL PART ONLY -- "ada", not
# "ada@icloud.com". Set DRAFT_FROM as a var if you want drafts written From a
# full address.
IMAP_USER=

# App-specific password for that mailbox. iCloud: appleid.apple.com ->
# Sign-In and Security -> App-Specific Passwords. It grants FULL mailbox access
# including SMTP send, so treat it as equivalent to the account password and
# rotate it by revoking the old one. It never reaches a log line (src/log.ts).
IMAP_PASSWORD=

# The bearer token MCP clients present. Generate one:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# This is the whole authentication gate until Cloudflare Access is configured,
# so make it random rather than memorable. Rotate with:
#   pnpm exec wrangler secret put MCP_API_KEY
MCP_API_KEY=
